<title>USA: Texaco fire pushes up US Northwest gasoline prices.</title>
<headline>Texaco fire pushes up US Northwest gasoline prices.</headline>
<dateline>SEATTLE 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>A morning fire at Texaco's Los Angeles-area refinery pushed up wholesale gasoline prices in the U.S. Northwest, traders said.</p>
<p>The fire broke out in the refinery's hydrotreating unit, leaving some traders speculating that the 96,000 barrel-per-day refinery could lose a significant part of its gasoline output.</p>
<p>Conventional-grade California gasoline rose two cents Monday as traders upped their buying prices to lock up supply.</p>
<p>Seattle conventional regular gasoline climbed in sympathy with southern California, advancing a half cent to 59/59.50 cents a gallon.</p>
<p>Distillate prices remained unchanged, with Texaco traders avoiding the spot market, brokers said.</p>
</text>
